Feature: pages-source-binding

  @FA-90 @build
  Scenario: Kernel adoption and live evidence bind the actual source and deployed bytes
    Given a signed Pages kernel produced at an exact source and complete build input identity
    When the current triggering source adopts it or the deployed site reuses live evidence
    Then a different producer source is accepted only when the signed holo and complete build inputs match
    And stale triggering runs, changed branch heads, altered claims and old artifacts are refused
    And a skipped deployment cannot run live verification or save live evidence
    And deployed bytes and identity must remain bound throughout live verification and cache reuse
    And the non-force push and full required acceptance gates remain mandatory
    And hosted canonical generation emits only a source and SDK bound reviewed patch without accepting uncommitted generated bytes
